cpcsekar@yahoo.com (CP Chandrasekar) writes:

[Please try to reduce your line length a bit.  TIA.]
> So, when one plays a wiz/monk and tanks up on armour, one loses 
> spell casting.  Therefore, a simpleton question.. Does this mean 
> that spellcasting is not used largely in high levels (because one 
> assumes that you need to be tanked up to touch these levels) at all?

First, the spellcasting proficiency will also improve, 
hence the hindrance of armor will decrease.  Second, 
there are some kinds of armor (mostly very good ones) 
which do not hinder spellcasting at all, or very little.  
Third, for some spells you usually have plenty of time 
to strip before casting.  In summary, with some skillful 
playing, you can have a good AC and good spellcasting 
chances at once.  

